# Per-machine repo list for bin/repo-sync.
# One `key=value` per line. '~' expands to $HOME. '#' starts a comment to end of line.
# This file is NOT committed, copy it to your config dir and edit per machine:
#   ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/repo-sync/repos.conf
#
# Recognized keys: repo, skip. Anything else is ignored.
# Keys repeat, one line per path.
#
# `repo` is a checkout to pull. repo-sync only pulls it when it is a git repo, sits on its
# own default branch and has a clean tree — anything else is reported and skipped.
# repo=~/instructions
# repo=~/some/other/checkout

# The dotfiles checkout this script was installed from needs no entry here — repo-sync finds
# it from its own location and always syncs it. Add a `skip` line for it to opt out.

# `skip` is a path you chose not to sync. It is listed in the output so it never looks
# like the repo was forgotten.
# skip=~/instructions-private

# Paths must be absolute or '~'-prefixed. A relative one would mean a different directory
# depending on where repo-sync was run from, so it is ignored with a warning.
#
# With no repo and no skip line here, repo-sync falls back to its built-in defaults,
# ~/instructions and ~/instructions-private. A missing path is asked about on a terminal:
# an alternative path or a permanent skip is recorded in this file and stops the question,
# while leaving it for now records no answer and asks again next time.
